WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.079
Rat and Mole ate in Badger's warm kitchen.

2
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:11.368
No one spoke until the plates were empty.

3
00:00:11.369 --> 00:00:15.156
"We're sorry that we bothered you," said Rat.

4
00:00:15.157 --> 00:00:19.466
"I'm glad to help," said Badger.

5
00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:22.109
Badger gave them some tea.

6
00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.590
"Now tell me," said Badger.

7
00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:27.405
"How is Toad?"

8
00:00:27.406 --> 00:00:30.541
Rat was surprised.

9
00:00:30.542 --> 00:00:35.898
Normally Badger did not talk about Riverbankers.

10
00:00:35.899 --> 00:00:40.634
"How's Toad?" said Rat. "Not good."

11
00:00:40.635 --> 00:00:44.600
"He crashed another car last week," said Mole.

12
00:00:44.601 --> 00:00:47.879
"He's a very bad driver," said Rat.

13
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.748
"But he thinks he's the best in the world."

14
00:00:51.749 --> 00:00:55.496
"How many has he had?" asked Badger.

15
00:00:55.497 --> 00:01:02.088
"Do you mean crashes or cars?" asked Mole.

16
00:01:02.089 --> 00:01:05.968
"It's the same thing," laughed Rat.

17
00:01:05.969 --> 00:01:12.426
"Seven! His yard is full of broken cars."

18
00:01:12.427 --> 00:01:16.646
"He went to the hospital three times," said Mole.

19
00:01:16.647 --> 00:01:20.677
"Soon he'll run out of money!" said Rat.

20
00:01:20.678 --> 00:01:23.340
"Or he'll get killed!"

21
00:01:23.341 --> 00:01:27.231
"Shouldn't we do something?" said Mole.

22
00:01:27.232 --> 00:01:30.178
Badger rubbed his chin.

23
00:01:30.179 --> 00:01:33.588
"The other animals will have to help.

24
00:01:33.589 --> 00:01:37.591
But we must wait until spring," he said.

25
00:01:37.592 --> 00:01:43.476
"In winter all the animals are too sleepy."

26
00:01:43.477 --> 00:01:46.945
Rat and Mole nodded.

27
00:01:46.946 --> 00:01:50.248
"I'm sleepy," said Rat.

28
00:01:50.249 --> 00:01:52.686
"It's time for bed."

29
00:01:52.687 --> 00:01:57.360
"I'm sleepy too," yawned Mole.

30
00:01:57.361 --> 00:02:01.296
"Come along," said Badger.

31
00:02:01.297 --> 00:02:05.483
Badger led them to their beds.

32
00:02:05.484 --> 00:02:07.487
Badger was right.

33
00:02:07.488 --> 00:02:14.698
In winter animals can't do anything too active.

